⚠️ Error / Problem Faced

In our own testing the scanner worked, because we only used QR codes.

In the demo we pointed it at real product tags, and it either read nothing or picked up the QR code printed on the tag instead of the barcode.

Real retail tags use EAN-13 barcodes (the 1D kind with vertical lines), and the library was tuned for QR codes.

We also restarted the server once during the demo, and every bag and bill disappeared, because all data was kept only in memory.

✅ Resolution
Switched to "Type barcode" and catalog search during the demo, so the demo could continue.
Recorded the scanner problem as the top issue for the next iteration.
Recorded the data-loss problem as the second issue.
Added the feedback from the demo to the requirements:
Separate logins for customers and cashiers
A cash desk that handles only cash

🖼️ Project Picture

The "Add by code" sheet used as a fallback during the demo: typing the barcode finds the product directly.

💡 Learning

We learned to test with real-world inputs, not only with inputs we create ourselves.

We also learned that a manual fallback keeps the system usable when a feature like the camera fails.

